<Project>

  <!--
    Nudge.props - shared update check (namespace DooDesch.Nudge) for Schedule I MelonLoader mods.
    Lives in the public Stash repo (github.com/DooDesch-Mods/ScheduleOne-Stash).

    A mod opts in with EXACTLY ONE line - IMPORTANT: place it AFTER the mod's <Compile Remove="Stash/**/*.cs" />
    ItemGroup (CI checks the Stash out as a subfolder, so without the Remove the SDK glob would double-include
    the file this props adds):
        <Import Project="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../Stash/build/Nudge.props"
                Condition="Exists('$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../Stash/build/Nudge.props')" />

    Usage in the host mod: call DooDesch.Nudge.Nudge.Watch() once in OnInitializeMelon. It checks EVERY
    loaded mod, not just the host - MelonLoader already knows each mod's version and download link, so any
    mod declaring a github.com repo as its 5th MelonInfo argument is covered. One consumer is enough for a
    whole install; further copies stand down at runtime.

    The class is INTERNAL and compiled into each consumer assembly separately, so there is NO CS0436 risk even
    when one consumer references another consumer's DLL. It needs only MelonLoader and the BCL - no Harmony,
    no S1API, no Unity, no game types - and is identical for IL2CPP and Mono.

    Thunderstore builds (-p:StoreBuild=thunderstore) get NO_EXTERNAL_FETCH below, which compiles the endpoint,
    the HTTP client and the parser out of the shipped DLL and leaves Watch() a no-op. That keeps a store build
    free of any outbound URL, which the release workflows check for.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(StoreBuild)' == 'thunderstore'">
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);NO_EXTERNAL_FETCH</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\nudge\Nudge.cs" Link="Nudge\Nudge.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
